OL,3,CProgramme listings for TUE 28 APR
OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GEric Lu, winner of both the First
OL,6,     GPrize and Gold Medal at the 2025
OL,7,     GInternational Chopin Piano
OL,8,     GCompetition, performs some of the
OL,9,     Gmost beloved piano works by
OL,10,     GSchubert and Chopin.
OL,11,G2145FThe Essay: The Death and Life of
OL,12,     FChristopher Marlowe
OL,13,     GJerry Brotton explores how with
OL,14,     GDr Faustus, Kit Marlowe pushed
OL,15,     Gthe boundaries of what was
OL,16,     Gpermissible for Elizabethan drama
OL,17,     Gand its writers even further.
